description:
 This is a combined synopsis/solicitation for commercial items prepared in accordance with the format in FAR Part 12.&nbsp; This announcement constitutes the only solicitation; offers are being requested, and a separate written solicitation will not be issued.&nbsp; 

 The Mt. Baker-Snoqualmie National Forest has a requirement for ADA-accessible portable toilets to be delivered, installed and serviced at the Marblemount and Sauk boat launches. All serviced weekly. Services include: once a week pump out toilet tank/vault. Replace with clean blue type liquid ready for a week&rsquo;s use. Spray down interior, remove trash, and clean/sanitize. Re-stock toilet paper and hand sanitizer. The Contractor shall furnish all labor, materials, equipment, tools, transportation, and supplies. 

Solicitation number 1240BD27Q0017 is issued as a Request for Quotation (RFQ). 

The sites are located on the Darrington Ranger District within Snohomish County and in the Mt. Baker Ranger District within Skagit County. See attached map listing in the Solicitation of Sauk River Boat Launch and Marblemount Boat Launch 

 The applicable North American Industry Classification Standard Code is 562991 Septic Tank and Related Services.&nbsp; The small business size standard is $9.0 Million. &nbsp;The Product Service code is S222 Housekeeping Waste Treatment Storage. This acquisition is a Total Small Business Set-Aside.&nbsp; All responsible sources may submit a quotation which will be considered by the agency.&nbsp; 

 The contract will be a Firm-Fixed Price contract with 1 base year and 4 Option Years for a possible total of 5 years. The period of performance will be: 

 Base Period&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;01/01/2027 &ndash; 12/31/2027 
Option Period 1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 01/01/2028 &ndash; 12/31/2028&nbsp;&nbsp; 
Option Period 2&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 01/01/2029 &ndash; 12/31/2029 &nbsp; 
Option Period 3&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 01/01/2030 &ndash; 12/31/2030 
Option Period 4&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 01/01/2031 &ndash; 12/31/2031 

 Address technical questions for this project to Ashley Ross at (360) 436-2316 or email ashley.ross@usda.gov &nbsp;  Address contracting questions to Contracting Officer Jorge Somoza at (509) 423-2224. Email jorge.somoza@usda.gov 

 Email your quote to jorge.somoza@usda.gov only. do not send your quote to anyone else. Submit your quote no later than 02 December 2026 before 2:00 PM PT. Any quote received after 2:00 PM on that day is late and it won&rsquo;t be accepted it.&nbsp;
